Unencoded tails always require raw padding, including compression fallback.

Compression can leave idata_type marked compressed before falling back to a
flat file. Without resetting it, erofs_write_tail_end pads the final raw page
at its beginning, shifting file content and dropping the same number of bytes
from the end. Establish the raw invariant where the unencoded tail is created.

--- a/lib/inode.c
+++ b/lib/inode.c
@@ -660,6 +660,7 @@ static int erofs_write_unencoded_data(struct erofs_inode *inode,
 	}
 
 	inode->idata_size = inode->i_size % erofs_blksiz(sbi);
+	inode->idata_type = EROFS_IDATA_TYPE_RAW;
 	remaining = inode->i_size - inode->idata_size;
 
 	ret = erofs_allocate_inode_bh_data(inode, remaining >> sbi->blkszbits,
